{"type":"text","timestamp":1778977300156,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb0bf13ffeMoQD0BmCaLT7Tp","part":{"id":"prt_e334f4ac0001e9dWmCCirtlihQ","messageID":"msg_e334f4210001K4psMzKS02Pob4","sessionID":"ses_1ccb0bf13ffeMoQD0BmCaLT7Tp","type":"text","text":"Reviewing the imported issue context and repository guidance first so I can determine the exact ontology change before editing.","time":{"start":1778977295040,"end":1778977300154}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977300162,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb0bf13ffeMoQD0BmCaLT7Tp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ZlTWiRf1DO1etkfJIGYWYGXr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/AGENTS.md","offset":1,"limit":260},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # CL Ontology Project Guide\n2: \n3: This includes instructions for editing the cl ontology. \n4: \n5: ## Project Layout\n6: - Main development file is `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` (functional syntax, one line per axiom).  ONLY EDIT THIS FILE, or files under docs/.\n7: - ODK and ontology documentation can be found in `/docs/`\n8: \n9: ## Querying ontology\n10: \n11: - Use grep/rg to find terms. Exploit the fact that typically it is one axiom per line\n12:     - `grep -i CL_0004177 src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` - all axioms that mention CL_0004177\n13:     - `grep 'AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label \"neuron\"' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` - the label axiom for neuron can be used to find the ID of neuron.\n14: - Only search over `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`\n15: - DO NOT bother doing your own greps over the file, or looking for other files, unless otherwise asked, you will just waste time.\n16: - ONLY use the methods above for searching the ontology\n17: \n18: ## Before making edits\n19: - Read the request carefully and make a plan, especially if there is nuance\n20: - If related issues are mentioned read them: `gh issue view GITHUB-ISSUE-NUMBER`\n21: - if a PMID is mentioned in the issue, ALWAYS try and read it\n22: - ALWAYS check proposed parent terms for consistency\n23: - For terms that are compositional, check `src/patterns/dosdp-patterns/*.yaml`\n24: - When generating a textual definition for a term, make sure to include in-line references if there are in the text on the ticket.\n25: \n26: ## Editors guide\n27: - design patterns are in docs/patterns\n28: - a guide to what relations to use for recording locations, properties etc can be found in docs/relations_guide.md\n29: \n30: \n31: ## OBO Guidelines\n32: - Term ID format: CL_NNNNNNN (7-digit number)\n33: - Handling New Term Requests (NTRs):\n34:   - New term IDs MUST start with CL_99xxxxx (as specified in Datatype: idrange:81 in src/ontology/cl-idranges.owl)\n35: - Each term requires: id, name, definition with references\n36: - Never guess CL IDs, or ontology term IDs, use search tools above to determine actual term\n37: - Never guess PMIDs for references, do a web search if needed\n38: - Use standard relationship types: is_a, part_of, has_part, etc.\n39: - Follow existing term patterns for consistency\n40: \n41: ## Publications\n42: - Run the command `aurelian fulltext <PMID:nnn>` to fetch full text for a publication. A doi or URL can also be used\n43: - You should cite publications appropriately, e.g. `def: \"....\" [PMID:nnnn, doi:mmmm]\n44: \n45: ## GitHub Contribution Process\n46: - most requests from users should follow one of two patterns:\n47:     - you are not confident how to proceed, in which case end with asking a clarifying question (via `gh`)\n48:     - you are confident how to proceed, you make changes, commit on a branch, and open a PR for the user to review\n49: - Check existing terms before adding new ones\n50: - For new terms: provide name, definition, place in hierarchy, and references\n51: - Include PMIDs for all assertions\n52: - Follow naming conventions from parent terms\n53: - always commit in a branch, e.g. issue-NNN\n54: - if there is an existing PR which you started then checkout that branch and continue, rather than starting a new PR (unless you explicitly want to abandon the original PR, e.g. it was on completely the wrong tracks)\n55: - always make clear detailed commit messages, saying what you did and why\n56: - always sign your commits `GitHub Copilot`\n57: - create PRs using `gh pr create ...`\n58: - File PRs with clear descriptions, and sign your PR\n59: \n60: ## Handling GitHub issues and requests\n61: - Use `gh` to read and write issues/PRs\n62: - Sign all commits and PRs as `GitHub Copilot`\n63: \n64: ## TROUBLESHOOTING\n65: \n66: - if your obo file has syntax errors, you can use `robot convert -vvv` to see full trace\n67: - use `robot reason` to validate\n68: \n69: ## Obsoleting terms\n70: \n71: obsolete terms should have no logical axioms (e.g. SubClassOf, EquivalentClasses) on them. Obsolete terms may be replaced by a single\n72: term (so-called obsoletion with exact replacement), or by zero to many `consider` tags.\n73: \n74: Synonyms and xrefs can be migrated judiciously,\n75: \n76: We never do complete merges now, so there should be no `alt_ids` or\n77: disappearing stanzas. If a user asks for a merge, they usually mean\n78: obsoletion with direct replacement.\n79: \n80: No relationship should point to an obsolete term - when you obsolete a term, you may need to also rewire\n81: terms to \"skip\" the obsoleted term.\n82: \n83: ## Other metadata\n84: \n85: - Link back to the issue you are dealing with using the `term_tracker_item`\n86: - All terms should have definitions, with at least one definition xref, ideally a PMID\n87: - All new terms MUST have a timestamp using Dublin Core terms date, e.g.\n88:   `AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4072102 \"2025-04-29T13:06:36Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)` (where terms: is a prefix for http://purl.org/dc/terms/)\n89: - You can sign terms as `dc:creator \"GitHub Copilot\"` only when creating new terms. You should not add yourself as a creator if you are editing existing terms.\n90: - If one or more ORCID are provided these MUST be added as Dublin Core Terms contributor axioms, e.g. `AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0000118 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2825-0621>)`\n91: \n92: ```\n93: # Class: obo:CL_4072102 (Purkinje layer interneuron)\n94: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35803588\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072102 \"A type of GABAergic interneuron residing in the Purkinje cell layer of the cerebellar cortex.\")\n95: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4072102 \"2025-04-29T13:06:36Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n96: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35803588\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072102 \"PLI\")\n97: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072102 \"Purkinje layer interneuron\")\n98: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4072102 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002979)))\n99: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072102 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n100: ```\n101: \n102: \n103: No relationship should point to an obsolete term - when you obsolete a term, you may need to also rewire\n104: terms to \"skip\" the obsoleted term.\n105: \n106: ## Other metadata\n107: \n108: - Link back to the issue you are dealing with using the `term_tracker_item`\n109: - All terms should have definitions, with at least one definition xref, ideally a PMID\n110: - You can sign terms as `terms:creator \"GitHub Copilot\"` only when creating new terms. You should not add yourself as a creator if you are editing existing terms. (Note: terms: is the prefix for http://purl.org/dc/terms/)\n111: \n112: \n113: ## Relationships\n114: \n115: All terms should have at least one \"is_a\" (SubClassOf to a named class) -- (this can be implicit by a logical definition, see below).\n116: Many terms in this ontology have part_of relationships to UBERON.\n117: \n118: ## Logical definitions\n119: \n120: These should follow genus-differentia form, and the text definition should mirror the logical definition. Example:\n121: \n122: ```\n123: # Class: obo:CL_4072102 (Purkinje layer interneuron)\n124: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35803588\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072102 \"A type of GABAergic interneuron residing in the Purkinje cell layer of the cerebellar cortex.\")\n125: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4072102 \"2025-04-29T13:06:36Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n126: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35803588\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072102 \"PLI\")\n127: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072102 \"Purkinje layer interneuron\")\n128: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4072102 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002979)))\n129: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072102 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n130: ```\n131: \n132: The reasoner can find the most specific `is_a`, so it's OK to leave this off.\n133: \n\n(End of file - total 133 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# CL Ontology Project Guide\n\nThis includes instructions for editing the cl ontology. \n\n## Project Layout\n- Main development file is `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` (functional syntax, one line per axiom).  ONLY EDIT THIS FILE, or files under docs/.\n- ODK and ontology documentation can be found in `/docs/`\n\n## Querying ontology\n\n- Use grep/rg to find terms. Exploit the fact that typically it is one axiom per line\n    - `grep -i CL_0004177 src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` - all axioms that mention CL_0004177\n    - `grep 'AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label \"neuron\"' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` - the label axiom for neuron can be used to find the ID of neuron.\n- Only search over `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`\n- DO NOT bother doing your own greps over the file, or looking for other files, unless otherwise asked, you will just waste time.\n- ONLY use the methods above for searching the ontology\n\n## Before making edits\n- Read the request carefully and make a plan, especially if there is nuance\n- If related issues are mentioned read them: `gh issue view GITHUB-ISSUE-NUMBER`","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1778977300125,"end":1778977300160}},"id":"prt_e334f5e97001mqtWhb92J02bUl","sessionID":"ses_1ccb0bf13ffeMoQD0BmCaLT7Tp","messageID":"msg_e334f4210001K4psMzKS02Pob4"}}
