{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977428910,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb0bf13ffeMoQD0BmCaLT7Tp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Vb7nFQ6MqcH1M3raFEClvbq5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Summary:\n+- reclassified `tendon cell` from tendon fibrocyte to tendon fibroblast and updated its textual definition to match\n+- reclassified `otic fibrocyte` from `fibrocyte` to `mesenchymal cell`\n+- updated the `otic fibrocyte` definition and added `cochlear fibrocyte` and `spiral ligament fibrocyte` synonyms with PMID-backed annotations\n+\n+I kept the changes scoped to the two classes requested in this issue. The broader otic fibroblast / spiral ligament fibrocyte restructuring noted in the issue body was left for the separate follow-up ticket mentioned there.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the requested reclassification updates for issue #3239 in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Updated `CL_0000388 tendon cell` to be defined as a `fibroblast` that is `part of` some `tendon`, replacing the previous `fibrocyte`-based classification.\n+- Revised the `tendon cell` textual definition so the genus now matches the logical definition.\n+- Reclassified `CL_0002665 otic fibrocyte` from `fibrocyte` to `mesenchymal cell`, following the newer cochlear mesenchyme framing cited in PMID:37720106.\n+- Updated the `otic fibrocyte` textual definition to match the new parentage and corrected `adaptions` to `adaptations`.\n+- Added PMID-backed synonyms to `otic fibrocyte`:\n+  - exact synonym: `cochlear fibrocyte` (PMID:31866825)\n+  - related synonym: `spiral ligament fibrocyte` (PMID:33193034)\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue explicitly requested removal of both classes from under `fibrocyte`.\n+- `tendon cell` already follows a fibroblast-like usage pattern in the issue discussion, so switching its equivalence and asserted inferred parent to `fibroblast` is the minimal ontology correction.\n+- For `otic fibrocyte`, the newer literature describes these as cochlear otic mesenchyme-derived cells rather than supporting a fibrocyte parent as the organizing genus. I therefore moved only the direct parent to `mesenchymal cell` and left the broader subclass structure intact.\n+- I treated `cochlear fibrocyte` as exact, but `spiral ligament fibrocyte` as related, because the issue body notes that the current general term spans both spiral ligament and spiral limbus and that a more precise spiral ligament term should be handled separately.\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- checked the existing axioms for both target classes and their current parents before editing\n+- reviewed the cited PubMed abstracts for PMID:31866825, PMID:33193034, and PMID:37720106\n+- ran `robot convert --input src/ontology/cl-edit.owl --output /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn.owl` to confirm the edited ontology parses successfully\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+- [x] read imported issue context\n+- [x] updated only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`\n+- [x] kept the scope to the two classes requested here\n+- [x] validated syntax with ROBOT\n+- [x] committed only the ontology file\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Summary:\n+- reclassified `tendon cell` from tendon fibrocyte to tendon fibroblast and updated its textual definition to match\n+- reclassified `otic fibrocyte` from `fibrocyte` to `mesenchymal cell`\n+- updated the `otic fibrocyte` definition and added `cochlear fibrocyte` and `spiral ligament fibrocyte` synonyms with PMID-backed annotations\n+\n+I kept the changes scoped to the two classes requested in this issue. The broader otic fibroblast / spiral ligament fibrocyte restructuring noted in the issue body was left for the separate follow-up ticket mentioned there.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+Implemented the requested reclassification updates for issue #3239 in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Updated `CL_0000388 tendon cell` to be defined as a `fibroblast` that is `part of` some `tendon`, replacing the previous `fibrocyte`-based classification.\n+- Revised the `tendon cell` textual definition so the genus now matches the logical definition.\n+- Reclassified `CL_0002665 otic fibrocyte` from `fibrocyte` to `mesenchymal cell`, following the newer cochlear mesenchyme framing cited in PMID:37720106.\n+- Updated the `otic fibrocyte` textual definition to match the new parentage and corrected `adaptions` to `adaptations`.\n+- Added PMID-backed synonyms to `otic fibrocyte`:\n+  - exact synonym: `cochlear fibrocyte` (PMID:31866825)\n+  - related synonym: `spiral ligament fibrocyte` (PMID:33193034)\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue explicitly requested removal of both classes from under `fibrocyte`.\n+- `tendon cell` already follows a fibroblast-like usage pattern in the issue discussion, so switching its equivalence and asserted inferred parent to `fibroblast` is the minimal ontology correction.\n+- For `otic fibrocyte`, the newer literature describes these as cochlear otic mesenchyme-derived cells rather than supporting a fibrocyte parent as the organizing genus. I therefore moved only the direct parent to `mesenchymal cell` and left the broader subclass structure intact.\n+- I treated `cochlear fibrocyte` as exact, but `spiral ligament fibrocyte` as related, because the issue body notes that the current general term spans both spiral ligament and spiral limbus and that a more precise spiral ligament term should be handled separately.\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- checked the existing axioms for both target classes and their current parents before editing\n+- reviewed the cited PubMed abstracts for PMID:31866825, PMID:33193034, and PMID:37720106\n+- ran `robot convert --input src/ontology/cl-edit.owl --output /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn.owl` to confirm the edited ontology parses successfully\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+- [x] read imported issue context\n+- [x] updated only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`\n+- [x] kept the scope to the two classes requested here\n+- [x] validated syntax with ROBOT\n+- [x] committed only the ontology file\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","relativePath":"ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Summary:\n+- reclassified `tendon cell` from tendon fibrocyte to tendon fibroblast and updated its textual definition to match\n+- reclassified `otic fibrocyte` from `fibrocyte` to `mesenchymal cell`\n+- updated the `otic fibrocyte` definition and added `cochlear fibrocyte` and `spiral ligament fibrocyte` synonyms with PMID-backed annotations\n+\n+I kept the changes scoped to the two classes requested in this issue. The broader otic fibroblast / spiral ligament fibrocyte restructuring noted in the issue body was left for the separate follow-up ticket mentioned there.\n","additions":8,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md","relativePath